Package: hexamap
Title: Hexagonal Heatmaps for Age-Period-Cohort Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Hawre", "Jalal", , "hjalal@uottawa.ca", role = "aut"),
    person("Fernando", "Alarid-Escudero", , "falarid@stanford.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: Visualize age-period-cohort (APC) data with hexamaps, a field
    of hexagonal tiles that places the age, period and cohort axes at equal
    60 degree angles. Unlike the traditional Lexis diagram, a hexamap does not
    compress patterns between adjacent cohorts or stretch patterns within a
    cohort, and adjacent tiles along every axis share a full edge. Implements
    the method described in Jalal and Burke (2020)
    <doi:10.1097/EDE.0000000000001236>.
